// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
// Glasnost's own rules patch layer "Pathing and other fixes" (M8 step C7). It holds no game
// data: it only sets quirk switches of our rules format to their off position, the behaviour
// each switch's spec states for that position (PLAN.md D6 and 4.6). The defaults in
// crates/deterministic/rules/src/quirks.rs stay the original's behaviour (D6, D8); this layer
// is an option of the client's new-game setup and network lobby, applied through
// `glasnost_rules::resolve_ruleset` as a mod patch layer, so it is part of `sim_rules_hash`.
//
// An entry is admitted only when (1) an approved spec states the switch's off position and the
// engine implements it, (2) the on position reads as a bug in play (a unit stuck, giving up,
// never moving, or a visible glitch), named by a play note or a request, and (3) it is not a
// balance change (D14). Each entry cites its claim and what it answers. The list is kept short;
// docs/development.md (Pathing and other fixes, M8 step C7) gives the entries considered and
// rejected.
{
  "globals": {
    "quirks": {
      // S-0212 claim 13 and Edge cases (quirks.corridor_retry_no_fallback off): when the new
      // coarse search after a corridor retry fails, one more cell search without a corridor is
      // made, with the same limits as the others, and the path computation fails only if it
      // fails too. On (the original), the computation fails and the unit gives up at once
      // although an open way round exists (claim 23 row 2).
      // Answers: the spec's own Edge case (a short strip of ground the unit cannot enter, open
      // to the coarse searches, fails at some alignments; off, it is passed at every one).
      // Pathing reports 1 and 2 (docs/m8-claims/a4-play-notes.md), Q-1771 and Q-1870, for
      // which this entry was admitted, are answered by S-0212 r82: the original finds the way
      // out of its own base on the first cell search, and this entry changes nothing there.
      "corridor_retry_no_fallback": false,
      // S-0212 claim 13a and Edge cases (quirks.corridor_split_probe off): the progress sector
      // counts as split when some cell of it inside the usable area is not in the free part,
      // and as whole otherwise; at a short strip the failure is expected at fewer alignments.
      // Admitted for pathing reports 1 and 2 (Q-1771, Q-1870) together with the entry above;
      // since S-0212 r82 those reports' shapes are passed on the first cell search, and with
      // the entry above off a strip is passed at every alignment whatever this switch says.
      // Kept until the lead rules on it (docs/m8-claims/c7-play-fixes.md, After intake 34).
      "corridor_split_probe": false,
      // S-0314 Edge cases (Hovering vehicle stranded) and Terms, What ends it
      // (quirks.depot_loss_strands_hover off): losing contact with a depot ends being settled,
      // so a hovering vehicle is switched on again and rises. On (the original), a hover whose
      // depot is destroyed or sold after it became settled never moves again once down
      // (claim 22), and so does one ordered away while it still sinks at a depot that comes
      // down outside the depot's cells: its order released the contact, and no later order
      // ends being settled there. Off, that order's release (claim 20), or the end of service
      // for a docked hover, ends it.
      // Answers: the play seam of docs/m8-claims/intake30-S-0314.md (a hover that never moves
      // again) and the spec's own Edge case.
      "depot_loss_strands_hover": false,
    },
  },
}
